/* ============================================================================
   Progressive Supranuclear Palsy (PSP) — a 4R tauopathy
   Quantitative Systems Pharmacology mechanistic map
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   ORGANISING IDEA (read this before reading the graph)
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Two trials in this disease reported target-engagement numbers that point in
   the OPPOSITE direction from their clinical results, and the ratio between
   those two numbers is the whole model.

     GOSURANEMAB (PASSPORT, n=486, Dam 2021 Nat Med)
       CSF unbound N-terminal tau  -98%   (placebo +11%, p<0.0001)
       PSPRS at week 52            10.4 vs 10.6   (p=0.85)
       CSF NfL                     unchanged
       -> The largest target-engagement number ever reported in a tauopathy
          trial, attached to the flattest null.

     NIO752 (MAPT antisense oligonucleotide, phase 1, n=59 PSP-RS)
       CSF total tau and p-tau181  -20%   (five times SMALLER)
       CSF NfL                     stabilised (placebo +40%)
       -> The smallest biomarker movement in the disease's history is attached
          to its only downstream signal, and it has gone to phase 3 (Preserve,
          n=300, 72 weeks, mPSPRS-10).

   A model in which "tau lowering" is ONE axis cannot hold both facts.  This
   map is therefore drawn so that tau exists in pools that differ by three to
   four orders of magnitude in SIZE and by everything in CAUSAL ROLE, and so
   that the two trials are seen to have moved two different pools.

   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   AXIS 1 — POOL SIZE.  The extracellular pool is the exhaust, not the engine.
   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
       intraneuronal soluble tau      ~2000 nM      (cluster cl_tau_intra)
       intraneuronal aggregated tau   ~1000-4000 nM tau-equivalents
       interstitial fluid (ISF) tau   ~1 nM         (cluster cl_extra)
       CSF tau                        ~0.01 nM
   F_EXT = ISF / intraneuronal  ~ 5e-4.  Removing 98% of the ISF pool removes
   ~0.05% of brain tau.  The ceiling on ANY extracellular-only mechanism is
   F_EXT, at any dose and any affinity.  Node CEILING_EXT states it.

   The inversion that makes this map worth drawing: a 150 kDa IgG partitions
   into brain at ~0.1-0.2% of plasma, so 2000 mg q4w yields an ISF antibody
   concentration of order 1-10 nM.  That saturates a 1 nM antigen and is
   irrelevant to a 2000 nM one.  98% ENGAGEMENT IS ITSELF THE EVIDENCE THAT
   THE POOL WAS SMALL.  (edges AB_ISF -> ETAU_N, node ENGAGE_PARADOX)

   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   AXIS 2 — EPITOPE.  The measured species and the causal species are different
            molecules, and the trials measured the decoy.
   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Tau in ISF/CSF is fragmented.  Two extracellular species are drawn as two
   physically separate nodes:
       ETAU_N  N-terminal fragments — ABUNDANT, cleaved by caspase-3/calpain/
               AEP, NOT seeding-competent.  This is literally what the assay
               "unbound N-terminal tau" reports.
       ETAU_S  mid-domain / MTBR assemblies — SCARCE, seeding-competent, and
               they have LOST the N-terminus.
   An N-terminal antibody has high affinity for the first and ~none for the
   second.  One epitope parameter then produces -98% of the measured species
   and 0% of the causal one.  The map names the discriminating assays:
   CSF SEEDING ACTIVITY (biosensor/RT-QuIC) and MTBR-tau243 — not total tau,
   not N-terminal tau.  (nodes ASSAY_WRONG, ASSAY_RIGHT)

   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   AXIS 3 — GEOMETRY.  Progression is a TRAVELLING WAVE through the connectome,
            so local aggregation kinetics are already saturated.
   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   The PSPRS slope is ~10-11 points/year and is close to LINEAR for years.
   Local templated seeding is autocatalytic (dA/dt = k*A*(M-A)) and is therefore
   LOGISTIC, i.e. sigmoid and saturating, in each region.  A sum of saturating
   sigmoids is linear only if regions are RECRUITED SEQUENTIALLY at a constant
   rate.  Linearity is thus evidence of a front moving through connectome space
   at constant velocity, with every already-involved nucleus at plateau.
   (cluster cl_wave; the region chain STN -> GPi/SNr -> midbrain tegmentum ->
   PPN -> dentate -> frontal cortex carries the front)

   Everything therapeutic follows from Fisher-KPP:   v  ~  sqrt(D * k * M)

     * Reduce LOCAL k (GSK-3beta inhibition, OGA inhibition, microtubule
       stabilisation) — you are moving a SATURATED quantity.  Predicted effect
       on the slope ~0.  This is tideglusib (TAUROS), davunetide (AL-108-231)
       and the OGA class, three nulls from one structural statement.
       (node SATURATED, edges marked "inert")
     * Reduce MONOMER M (MAPT ASO) — v falls as sqrt(M).  20% CSF tau lowering
       corresponds to ~35-40% front-region knockdown and ~20% slope reduction.
       THE SQUARE ROOT IS THE PUNCHLINE: to HALVE the slope you must remove
       ~75% of tau.  That is a statement about dose, not about drug.
       (node SQRT_LAW)
     * Reduce TRANSFER D or its accessible fraction PHI_ACC (uptake blockade,
       mid-domain/MTBR antibody, exosome/TNT routes) — v falls as sqrt(D), and
       this is the only class whose ceiling is not F_EXT... but only for the
       part of the transfer flux that is exposed to bulk ISF.  PHI_ACC is drawn
       as an explicit gate, because trans-synaptic microdomains, tunnelling
       nanotubes and exosome-encapsulated transfer are NOT antibody-accessible.
       (cluster cl_uptake, node PHI_ACC)

   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   AXIS 4 — TIMING.  The score is a delayed, reserve-gated INTEGRAL of neuron
            loss, so a 52-week trial in symptomatic PSP is underpowered by
            construction rather than by sample size.
   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Aggregate load does not cause the score; it causes a loss rate, which
   integrates into neuron count, which crosses reserve thresholds, which move
   the score.  Two integrations and one threshold sit between drug and endpoint.
   At enrolment the load-bearing nuclei are already 40-60% depleted, so the
   CURRENT slope is set by damage already committed and a drug can only bend
   what has not happened yet.  Blocking 100% of new aggregation for 52 weeks
   from enrolment buys a couple of PSPRS points; the same block three years
   pre-symptomatically buys most of the disease.
   (cluster cl_endpoints, nodes LAG1/LAG2/RESERVE, node POWER_TRAP)

   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   AXIS 5 — WHICH NUCLEI.  Vertical gaze palsy and early falls are not
            "symptoms of PSP"; they are the two lowest-reserve nuclei, and one
            of them is an UNTHRESHOLDED readout.
   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Vertical saccade peak velocity is proportional to surviving riMLF burst
   neurons with essentially no reserve, so it is the earliest and most
   sensitive marker — and it FLOORS first, which is why oculomotor PSPRS items
   stop moving while the disease continues.  PPN cholinergic loss gives falls
   within the first year.  (clusters cl_circuits, cl_endpoints)

   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   AXIS 6 — DEATH is competing-risk and is dominated by dysphagia.
   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   dCIF/dt = h*S, not summed hazards.  Aspiration pneumonia via bulbar failure
   is the dominant channel; PEG feeding moves one hazard and not the other.
   The RS/P subtype difference (survival ~7 vs ~10 years, slope ~11 vs ~5) is
   produced by the ORIGIN of the wave — midbrain tegmental vs nigrostriatal —
   and by connectome outflow, not by a severity knob.  (clusters cl_survival,
   cl_subtypes)
   ============================================================================ */

digraph PSP_QSP {
  graph [
    rankdir = TB,
    splines = spline,
    overlap = false,
    nodesep = 0.28,
    ranksep = 0.55,
    fontname = "Helvetica",
    fontsize = 11,
    labelloc = "t",
    label = <<b>Progressive Supranuclear Palsy (PSP) — QSP mechanistic map</b><br/>
      <i>4R-tau travelling wave through the connectome · pool-size ceiling on extracellular mechanisms · reserve-gated clinical readout</i><br/>
      <font point-size="10">pools differ by 10<sup>3</sup>-10<sup>4</sup>: intraneuronal ~2000 nM · ISF ~1 nM · CSF ~0.01 nM &nbsp;|&nbsp; v ~ sqrt(D·k·M) &nbsp;|&nbsp; PSPRS = reserve-gated integral of neuron loss</font>>,
    bgcolor = "white",
    compound = true,
    newrank = true
  ];
  node [fontname = "Helvetica", fontsize = 10, style = "filled", shape = "box",
        margin = "0.08,0.05", penwidth = 1.0];
  edge [fontname = "Helvetica", fontsize = 8, arrowsize = 0.65, penwidth = 1.0];

  /* ---- shared style vocabulary --------------------------------------------
     genes / transcripts  : ellipse, khaki
     protein species      : box, light blue
     aggregate species    : box, orange  (the causal chain)
     enzymes / PTM        : box, plum
     cells / glia         : box, light green
     anatomy / regions    : box3d, wheat
     drugs                : component, salmon
     PK compartments      : box, rosybrown, dashed
     biomarkers           : note, light yellow
     clinical endpoints   : hexagon, light coral
     structural claims    : parallelogram, grey  (things the model ASSERTS)
     trials               : note, white, dashed
     ---------------------------------------------------------------------- */

/* ==========================================================================
   1. GENETIC AND CONSTITUTIONAL RISK
   ========================================================================== */
subgraph cluster_genetics {
  label = "1 · Genetic & constitutional risk (sets M, k_agg, clearance capacity)";
  style = "filled"; color = "#f7f3e3"; fontsize = 12; fontcolor = "#6b5b16";
  node [fillcolor = "#f0e6a8", shape = "ellipse"];

  G_MAPT_H1     [label = "MAPT H1/H1c haplotype\n17q21.31 inversion\nOR ≈ 5.5 homozygous"];
  G_MAPT_UTR    [label = "MAPT 3'UTR / intron 9\nexpression-increasing alleles"];
  G_MAPT_RARE   [label = "rare MAPT variants\n(R5L, ΔN296, S305S)\n4R-shifting"];
  G_MOBP        [label = "MOBP 3p22\noligodendroglial\nmyelin basic protein"];
  G_STX6        [label = "STX6 1q25\nsyntaxin-6\nendosome-Golgi fusion"];
  G_EIF2AK3     [label = "EIF2AK3 2p11\nPERK / unfolded\nprotein response"];
  G_TRIM11      [label = "TRIM11 1q42\ntau disaggregase /\nSUMO-dependent"];
  G_DUSP10      [label = "DUSP10\nMAPK phosphatase"];
  G_SLCO1A2     [label = "SLCO1A2 / RUNX2\nsecondary GWAS loci"];
  G_APOE        [label = "APOE ε4\n(weak / absent in PSP —\nnot an amyloid disease)", fillcolor = "#e8e8e8"];
  AGE           [label = "age\n(onset 63-66 y)", fillcolor = "#e0d9b8"];
  SEX           [label = "sex M ≈ F", fillcolor = "#e0d9b8"];
  ENVIR         [label = "environmental / annonacin\n(Guadeloupe PSP-like)", fillcolor = "#e0d9b8"];
}

/* ==========================================================================
   2. MAPT TRANSCRIPTION, EXON-10 SPLICING, AND THE ASO TARGET
   ========================================================================== */
subgraph cluster_transcript {
  label = "2 · MAPT transcription & exon-10 splicing — the ONLY node that lowers monomer M";
  style = "filled"; color = "#eef4fb"; fontsize = 12; fontcolor = "#1d4f7c";
  node [fillcolor = "#cfe3f7"];

  MAPT_GENE  [label = "MAPT gene\n17q21.31", shape = "ellipse", fillcolor = "#f0e6a8"];
  SPLICE_F   [label = "splice factors\nSRSF1/2 · PTBP1 · TRA2B\nhnRNP-E2", fillcolor = "#e6d0f0"];
  EX10_IN    [label = "exon 10 INCLUDED\n→ 4R tau (0N/1N/2N-4R)", fillcolor = "#f8cf9c"];
  EX10_OUT   [label = "exon 10 skipped\n→ 3R tau"];
  R4R3       [label = "4R : 3R ratio\nPSP ≈ 4R-dominant\n(cf. Pick 3R, AD mixed)", shape = "parallelogram", fillcolor = "#d9d9d9"];
  MAPT_MRNA  [label = "MAPT mRNA\n(model state)", shape = "ellipse", fillcolor = "#f0e6a8"];
  TRANSL     [label = "translation"];
  RNASEH1    [label = "RNase H1\ncleaves ASO:mRNA duplex", fillcolor = "#e6d0f0"];
}

/* ==========================================================================
   3. INTRANEURONAL TAU — THE ENGINE (≈2000 nM)
   ========================================================================== */
subgraph cluster_tau_intra {
  label = "3 · Intraneuronal tau — THE ENGINE  ~2000 nM soluble + 1000-4000 nM aggregated";
  style = "filled"; color = "#fdf1e6"; fontsize = 12; fontcolor = "#8a4b12";
  node [fillcolor = "#f8cf9c"];

  TAU_MT     [label = "MT-bound tau\n(functional pool)", fillcolor = "#cfe3f7"];
  TAU_MON    [label = "free soluble 4R monomer\nM ≈ 2000 nM\n⟵ MODEL STATE", penwidth = 2.2, color = "#b35c00"];
  TAU_MISF   [label = "misfolded monomer\n(PHF6 / VQIVYK exposed)"];
  TAU_DIM    [label = "dimer / trimer"];
  TAU_OLIG   [label = "OLIGOMER\nseeding-competent,\nmost cytotoxic species", penwidth = 2.0];
  TAU_PFF    [label = "filament\n(PSP: straight, 4R fold —\ndistinct cryo-EM fold)"];
  NFT        [label = "globose neurofibrillary\ntangle (neurons)"];
  TUFT       [label = "TUFTED ASTROCYTE\n(pathognomonic for PSP)", fillcolor = "#c8e6c9"];
  OCB        [label = "oligodendroglial\ncoiled body", fillcolor = "#c8e6c9"];
  THREAD     [label = "neuropil threads"];
  SEED_UNIT  [label = "SEEDING UNIT\n(minimal templating assembly)", shape = "parallelogram", fillcolor = "#d9d9d9"];
  A_LOAD     [label = "regional aggregate load A_r\n⟵ MODEL STATE (×8 regions)", penwidth = 2.2, color = "#b35c00"];
}

/* ==========================================================================
   4. POST-TRANSLATIONAL MODIFICATION — where most drugs act, and where
      the model says the quantity is already saturated
   ========================================================================== */
subgraph cluster_ptm {
  label = "4 · Post-translational modification — most drugs act here, on a SATURATED quantity (AXIS 3)";
  style = "filled"; color = "#f6eefa"; fontsize = 12; fontcolor = "#5b2a72";
  node [fillcolor = "#e6d0f0"];

  GSK3B     [label = "GSK-3β\n⟵ MODEL STATE"];
  CDK5      [label = "CDK5 / p25\n(calpain-cleaved p35)"];
  DYRK1A    [label = "DYRK1A"];
  MARK      [label = "MARK / PAR-1\nKXGS motifs"];
  CK1D      [label = "CK1δ"];
  PP2A      [label = "PP2A (B55α)\nthe dominant tau phosphatase"];
  PTAU      [label = "hyperphosphorylated tau\nAT8 S202/T205 · pT231\npS396/404 · p181 · p217", fillcolor = "#f8cf9c"];
  DETACH    [label = "detachment from\nmicrotubules", shape = "parallelogram", fillcolor = "#d9d9d9"];
  OGT       [label = "OGT\nO-GlcNAc transferase"];
  OGA       [label = "OGA (MGEA5)\nO-GlcNAcase\n⟵ DRUG TARGET"];
  OGLCNAC   [label = "O-GlcNAc-tau\nS400 etc. — competes with\nphosphorylation, anti-aggregant"];
  P300      [label = "p300 / CBP\nacetyltransferase\n⟵ salsalate target"];
  SIRT1     [label = "SIRT1 / HDAC6\ndeacetylases"];
  ACTAU     [label = "acetyl-tau K174 / K274 / K280\nblocks degradation,\npromotes aggregation", fillcolor = "#f8cf9c"];
  CASP3     [label = "caspase-3\n→ D421 truncation"];
  CALPAIN   [label = "calpain-1"];
  AEP       [label = "AEP / legumain (LGMN)\n→ N368 truncation"];
  TRUNC     [label = "TRUNCATED tau\n— N-terminus LOST —\nseeding-competent core", fillcolor = "#f8cf9c", penwidth = 2.0];
  NTFRAG    [label = "N-TERMINAL FRAGMENTS\nabundant · NOT seeding-competent\n= the PASSPORT assay analyte", fillcolor = "#ffd9d9", penwidth = 2.0];
  UBIQ      [label = "ubiquitination\nK48 / K63"];
  SUMO      [label = "SUMOylation"];
  NITRO     [label = "nitration / glycation"];
}

/* ==========================================================================
   5. PROTEOSTASIS AND CLEARANCE — the compartment ASO and progranulin reach
   ========================================================================== */
subgraph cluster_clearance {
  label = "5 · Proteostasis — intracellular clearance (the compartment that matters)";
  style = "filled"; color = "#eefaf1"; fontsize = 12; fontcolor = "#1c6b3a";
  node [fillcolor = "#c8e6c9"];

  PROTEA   [label = "26S proteasome"];
  CHIP     [label = "HSP70 / HSP90 / CHIP\nco-chaperone triage"];
  BAG3     [label = "BAG3 / BAG1 route"];
  CMA      [label = "chaperone-mediated\nautophagy (LAMP2A)"];
  MACROAUT [label = "macroautophagy\nLC3-II / p62\n⟵ MODEL STATE"];
  MTORC1   [label = "mTORC1"];
  TFEB     [label = "TFEB\nlysosomal biogenesis"];
  LYSO     [label = "lysosome\nCTSD / CTSB / v-ATPase"];
  PGRN     [label = "progranulin (PGRN)\nlysosomal co-factor\n⟵ MODEL STATE · ezeprogind target", penwidth = 2.0];
  ROCK     [label = "ROCK1/2\n⟵ fasudil target", fillcolor = "#e6d0f0"];
  UPR      [label = "PERK / EIF2AK3\nUPR — risk locus"];
  TRIM11P  [label = "TRIM11\ndisaggregase activity"];
  CLR_TOT  [label = "TOTAL intracellular\nclearance capacity", shape = "parallelogram", fillcolor = "#d9d9d9"];
}

/* ==========================================================================
   6. THE EXTRACELLULAR POOL — the exhaust (~1 nM ISF, ~0.01 nM CSF)
   ========================================================================== */
subgraph cluster_extra {
  label = "6 · Extracellular tau — THE EXHAUST  ISF ~1 nM · CSF ~0.01 nM  (F_EXT ≈ 5×10⁻⁴)";
  style = "filled"; color = "#fdeaea"; fontsize = 12; fontcolor = "#8f2020";
  node [fillcolor = "#ffd9d9"];

  RELEASE_A  [label = "activity-dependent\nsynaptic release"];
  RELEASE_U  [label = "unconventional secretion\n(type III, PI(4,5)P2)"];
  EXOSOME    [label = "exosome / ectosome\nENCAPSULATED — antibody-inaccessible", penwidth = 1.8];
  TNT        [label = "tunnelling nanotube\ndirect cytoplasmic transfer —\nantibody-inaccessible", penwidth = 1.8];
  DEATH_REL  [label = "release from dying neurons"];
  ETAU_N     [label = "ETAU_N — ISF N-terminal fragments\n≈ 1 nM · NON-seeding\n⟵ MODEL STATE · the measured pool", penwidth = 2.4, color = "#8f2020"];
  ETAU_S     [label = "ETAU_S — ISF seed-competent\nmid-domain / MTBR assemblies\n≈ 0.01-0.05 nM · the CAUSAL pool", penwidth = 2.4, color = "#8f2020"];
  ISF_FLOW   [label = "ISF bulk flow"];
  GLYMPH     [label = "glymphatic / AQP4\nperivascular clearance"];
  CSF_N      [label = "CSF N-terminal tau\n(≈10 pM) ⟵ PASSPORT endpoint", shape = "note", fillcolor = "#fffbcc"];
  CSF_S      [label = "CSF seeding activity\n(biosensor / RT-QuIC)", shape = "note", fillcolor = "#fffbcc"];
  BLOOD_TAU  [label = "plasma tau / p-tau181", shape = "note", fillcolor = "#fffbcc"];
  F_EXT      [label = "F_EXT = ISF/intraneuronal ≈ 5×10⁻⁴", shape = "parallelogram", fillcolor = "#d9d9d9", penwidth = 2.0];
  CEILING_EXT[label = "CEILING: any extracellular-only\nmechanism is bounded by F_EXT ×\nΦ_ACC — at ANY dose or affinity", shape = "parallelogram", fillcolor = "#bdbdbd", penwidth = 2.4];
}

/* ==========================================================================
   7. UPTAKE AND TEMPLATED SEEDING — the transfer flux, and its accessible part
   ========================================================================== */
subgraph cluster_uptake {
  label = "7 · Uptake & templated seeding — transfer flux D, and the accessible fraction Φ_ACC";
  style = "filled"; color = "#eef4fb"; fontsize = 12; fontcolor = "#1d4f7c";
  node [fillcolor = "#cfe3f7"];

  HSPG      [label = "heparan sulphate\nproteoglycan (HS 6-O-S)"];
  LRP1      [label = "LRP1\ndominant tau uptake receptor"];
  M1M3      [label = "muscarinic M1/M3"];
  MACROPIN  [label = "macropinocytosis"];
  ENDOSOME  [label = "endosome"];
  ESCAPE    [label = "endosomal escape\n(membrane rupture, Gal3+)"];
  TEMPLATE  [label = "TEMPLATED CONVERSION\nmonomer → aggregate\n(autocatalytic: k·A·M)", shape = "parallelogram", fillcolor = "#d9d9d9", penwidth = 2.2];
  PHI_ACC   [label = "Φ_ACC — fraction of transfer flux\nexposed to bulk ISF\n(the rest: exosome, TNT, synaptic\nmicrodomain — not accessible)", shape = "parallelogram", fillcolor = "#bdbdbd", penwidth = 2.2];
  FRAGMENT  [label = "secondary fragmentation\n→ new seeding units"];
  SYN_CLEFT [label = "trans-synaptic cleft\nmicrodomain, short residence"];
}

/* ==========================================================================
   8. THE TRAVELLING WAVE — the geometry that makes the slope linear
   ========================================================================== */
subgraph cluster_wave {
  label = "8 · The TRAVELLING WAVE — why the PSPRS slope is linear and local kinetics are inert (AXIS 3)";
  style = "filled"; color = "#fff4e0"; fontsize = 12; fontcolor = "#7a4a00";
  node [fillcolor = "#ffe0b2"];

  LOGISTIC  [label = "local logistic saturation\nA_r → A_max within ~1.5-2 y", shape = "parallelogram", fillcolor = "#d9d9d9"];
  SATURATED [label = "SATURATED: A_r is at plateau\nin every already-involved nucleus\n⇒ Δk changes nothing", shape = "parallelogram", fillcolor = "#bdbdbd", penwidth = 2.4];
  CONNECTOME[label = "connectome weights W_rs\n(axonal, monosynaptic)"];
  FRONT     [label = "propagating FRONT\nsequential regional recruitment"];
  VELOCITY  [label = "wave velocity\nv ~ sqrt(D · k · M)", shape = "parallelogram", fillcolor = "#bdbdbd", penwidth = 2.4];
  LINEARITY [label = "EMERGENT: near-linear\nglobal score, 10-11 pts/y", shape = "parallelogram", fillcolor = "#d9d9d9", penwidth = 2.0];
  SQRT_LAW  [label = "MEASURED ELASTICITY, not an assumed law\ntreatment phase: dln(slope)/dln(M) = 0.02\n=> halving the slope is UNREACHABLE at\nany knockdown once symptoms exist\nprevention: 50% lifelong knockdown\ndelays trial-entry severity 4.1 years", shape = "parallelogram", fillcolor = "#bdbdbd", penwidth = 2.4];
  ORIGIN_RS [label = "wave origin: midbrain tegmentum\n/ STN → PSP-RS", shape = "parallelogram", fillcolor = "#d9d9d9"];
  ORIGIN_P  [label = "wave origin: SN / striatum,\nlow outflow → PSP-P", shape = "parallelogram", fillcolor = "#d9d9d9"];
}

/* ==========================================================================
   9. ANATOMY — the eight regions carrying the front
   ========================================================================== */
subgraph cluster_regions {
  label = "9 · Regional anatomy — the eight nuclei the model integrates separately";
  style = "filled"; color = "#f7f1e3"; fontsize = 12; fontcolor = "#6b4f16";
  node [fillcolor = "#f2e2bf", shape = "box3d"];

  R_STN    [label = "R1 · subthalamic nucleus\n(earliest, severe)"];
  R_GPI    [label = "R2 · GPi / SNr\n(GABAergic output)"];
  R_SNC    [label = "R3 · SNc dopaminergic\n(→ parkinsonism)"];
  R_MIDB   [label = "R4 · midbrain tegmentum\nriMLF + rip omnipause\n(→ vertical gaze)"];
  R_PPN    [label = "R5 · pedunculopontine n.\ncholinergic (→ falls)"];
  R_DENT   [label = "R6 · dentate nucleus /\nsuperior cerebellar peduncle"];
  R_FRONT  [label = "R7 · frontal cortex\n(dorsolateral + medial)"];
  R_LC     [label = "R8 · locus coeruleus /\nraphe / medullary bulbar"];
  MIDB_ATR [label = "midbrain atrophy\n(hummingbird sign)"];
  THAL     [label = "thalamus (relay)"];
  STRI     [label = "striatum"];
  M1       [label = "precentral cortex"];
}

/* ==========================================================================
   10. NEURONAL DEATH AND THE NfL SIGNAL
   ========================================================================== */
subgraph cluster_neurodeg {
  label = "10 · Neuronal injury & death — the integrator between tau and the score";
  style = "filled"; color = "#f2f2f2"; fontsize = 12; fontcolor = "#3a3a3a";
  node [fillcolor = "#dcdcdc"];

  SYNLOSS  [label = "synapse loss\n(SV2A ↓)"];
  AXTRANS  [label = "axonal transport failure\n(kinesin/dynein detachment)"];
  MITODYS  [label = "mitochondrial mislocalisation"];
  DENDRIT  [label = "dendritic simplification"];
  NEUR_R   [label = "surviving neurons N_r\n⟵ MODEL STATE (×8)", penwidth = 2.2, color = "#333333"];
  APOP     [label = "apoptosis / necroptosis\ncaspase-3, RIPK1"];
  NFL_REL  [label = "neurofilament light release"];
  RESERVE  [label = "REGIONAL RESERVE θ_r\nscore moves only when N_r\nfalls below threshold", shape = "parallelogram", fillcolor = "#bdbdbd", penwidth = 2.2];
}

/* ==========================================================================
   11. GLIA AND NEUROINFLAMMATION
   ========================================================================== */
subgraph cluster_glia {
  label = "11 · Glial response — amplifier, not initiator";
  style = "filled"; color = "#eefaf1"; fontsize = 12; fontcolor = "#1c6b3a";
  node [fillcolor = "#c8e6c9"];

  MG_HOM   [label = "homeostatic microglia\nP2RY12+ TMEM119+"];
